                {
                    "axis": "x",
                    "justification": "The x-axis is plotted on a logarithmic scale (tick labels shown at 0.01, 0.1, 1, 10, 100), but some points representing barcodes exclusively detected by one method are plotted at 0 (as described in the caption). Zero cannot be represented on a true log scale, so these points are placed at 0 outside the log sequence; there is no conventional visual axis-break marker (no zigzag or oblique lines) indicating this discontinuity."
                },
                {
                    "axis": "y",
                    "justification": "The y-axis likewise uses a logarithmic sequence of ticks but includes points plotted at 0 for barcodes exclusively detected by the other method. These zero values create an implicit discontinuity between the 0 position and the log-scaled tick sequence (0.01, 0.1, 1...), and there are no standard visual break markers to indicate the axis has been discontinuously represented."
                }
            ]
